1
00:25:38,390 --> 00:25:40,020
Really now?

2
00:25:40,020 --> 00:25:42,270
I'll take care of this, then!

3
00:25:42,270 --> 00:25:43,770
I'll leave the rest to you...

4
00:25:43,770 --> 00:25:44,610
Pythagoras!

5
00:25:44,610 --> 00:25:45,650
Excuse me?!

6
00:25:45,650 --> 00:25:46,650
Of course!

7
00:25:46,650 --> 00:25:50,530
You don't get interesting
battle data like this every day!

8
00:25:54,620 --> 00:25:56,870
I've got to draw up some blueprints!

9
00:25:56,870 --> 00:25:58,120
So busy, so busy!

10
00:25:58,120 --> 00:26:00,250
I'd even take help from a cat at this point!

11
00:26:08,630 --> 00:26:09,880
Wonderful!

12
00:26:11,260 --> 00:26:12,930
Excellent!

13
00:26:12,930 --> 00:26:16,600
The seraphim's attack patterns
are developing as he grows!

14
00:26:16,600 --> 00:26:21,180
Could this support my theory that experiences
are stored in one's hereditary elements?

15
00:26:21,180 --> 00:26:22,310
Come on!

16
00:26:22,310 --> 00:26:24,230
Really give it to 'em!

17
00:26:24,230 --> 00:26:26,980
S-Shark!

18
00:26:27,770 --> 00:26:31,530
This could be the solution to
the accelerated growth issue!

19
00:26:31,530 --> 00:26:35,740
Heart rate over 90 BPM!
Green blood is flowing faster!

20
00:26:38,540 --> 00:26:43,080
Show 'em what you're made of!

21
00:26:56,050 --> 00:26:56,930
York the Greedy

22
00:27:01,100 --> 00:27:02,560
The more I write...

23
00:27:03,230 --> 00:27:04,940
the more my stomach growls!

24
00:27:06,150 --> 00:27:07,810
There's no stoppin' these ideas!

25
00:27:07,810 --> 00:27:09,400
I ain't got time to eat!

26
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:12,030
I need you to chow down for me, York!

27
00:27:13,780 --> 00:27:16,410
Okay!

28
00:27:20,120 --> 00:27:23,540
That's the ticket! My noggin
is soakin' up the nutrients!

29
00:27:23,540 --> 00:27:25,870
I've got even more ideas!

30
00:27:26,960 --> 00:27:29,290
Eat! Eat! York!

31
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:33,550
Another helping for you, Dr. York.

32
00:27:38,010 --> 00:27:40,010
Nuh-uh, not enough!

33
00:27:40,010 --> 00:27:41,760
Get me more!

34
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:44,350
Yes, doctor! Right away!

35
00:27:52,320 --> 00:27:54,610
Yummy!

36
00:27:54,610 --> 00:27:57,570
Her current BMI is over 600!

37
00:27:57,570 --> 00:27:59,820
I don't want any more!

38
00:28:00,780 --> 00:28:02,990
That's it, S-Shark!

39
00:28:02,990 --> 00:28:06,460
The battle data keeps updating!

40
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:11,420
Oh no, not now...!

41
00:28:15,170 --> 00:28:19,050
Ow, ow... I'm calling a temporary truce!

42
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:22,640
I can't miss this opportunity
to monitor his growth!

43
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:26,600
I gotta go to the bathroom,
but I can't waste any time!

44
00:28:33,570 --> 00:28:35,280
Much better!

45
00:28:36,950 --> 00:28:40,490
Digestion Punch!

46
00:28:43,280 --> 00:28:45,410
That's it! Time to experiment!

47
00:28:45,410 --> 00:28:48,370
Please bring me all materials
relating to devil fruits!

48
00:28:48,370 --> 00:28:51,000
Deliver everything to Dr. Pythagoras!

49
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,750
Prep for Dr. Edison's experiment!

50
00:28:52,750 --> 00:28:55,260
To simulation room 88!

51
00:28:56,630 --> 00:28:57,840
Nap time.

52
00:29:00,590 --> 00:29:04,890
That's Dr. York's fourth
snack, dump, nap cycle today!

53
00:29:14,770 --> 00:29:15,780
Are you serious?!

54
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:25,910
That's enough, seraphim.

55
00:29:25,910 --> 00:29:26,740
Stand down.

56
00:29:27,790 --> 00:29:29,870
Edison, Lilith, Pythagoras!

57
00:29:30,330 --> 00:29:31,750
I think you've had enough.

58
00:29:31,750 --> 00:29:33,840
Oh, what a shame...

59
00:29:33,840 --> 00:29:35,590
Consarn it!

60
00:29:35,590 --> 00:29:36,960
Ouch!

61
00:29:36,960 --> 00:29:38,630
Why's that scoundrel butting in?!

62
00:29:38,630 --> 00:29:40,680
We were just getting to the good part!

63
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:42,300
Eureka!

64
00:29:51,350 --> 00:29:54,230
Did that guy come to rescue us?

65
00:29:54,230 --> 00:29:56,610
No way, he's just as shady
as the rest of them!

66
00:29:56,610 --> 00:29:59,110
He's probably a colleague of Lilith's.

67
00:29:59,110 --> 00:30:01,610
So this guy must be...

68
00:30:01,610 --> 00:30:04,530
I am Dr. Vegapunk Shaka.

69
00:30:04,950 --> 00:30:08,040
Shaka the Just

70
00:30:08,870 --> 00:30:10,500
Another one?!

71
00:30:10,500 --> 00:30:12,250
What's with you guys?!

72
00:30:12,830 --> 00:30:15,170
You must be the Straw Hat Pirates.

73
00:30:15,170 --> 00:30:17,630
We are! Now tell us what's
wrong with these shoes!

74
00:30:17,630 --> 00:30:19,590
They're stuck to the floor!

75
00:30:19,590 --> 00:30:23,590
Dom shoes can easily be controlled
by the magnets in the laboratory.

76
00:30:23,970 --> 00:30:25,800
So resistance is futile, then.

77
00:30:26,430 --> 00:30:28,930
We can't trust pirates.

78
00:30:28,930 --> 00:30:33,770
There was also a female Vegapunk,
and another that was talking over the speakers...

79
00:30:33,770 --> 00:30:34,810
Yeah...

80
00:30:34,810 --> 00:30:36,860
I am Vegapunk as well.

81
00:30:36,860 --> 00:30:38,730
I don't get it!

82
00:30:38,730 --> 00:30:40,740
How many of you guys are there?!

83
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:42,490
Maybe I'm Vegapunk, too...

84
00:30:42,490 --> 00:30:43,490
What?!

85
00:30:43,490 --> 00:30:46,240
Like hell you are!

86
00:30:50,660 --> 00:30:54,370
Does this island look like
the future to all of you?

87
00:30:54,370 --> 00:30:56,880
Yeah, it's amazing!

88
00:30:56,880 --> 00:30:58,380
It's not just any future!

89
00:30:58,380 --> 00:31:00,460
There were those mechanical sea beasts!

90
00:31:01,130 --> 00:31:04,880
Plus, the Vegaforce-01
and the island A.C. system, too!

91
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:06,930
It's a hell of a future!

92
00:31:06,930 --> 00:31:09,890
And I've never seen a city like that...

93
00:31:09,890 --> 00:31:14,890
I wanna snoop around
and see how everything works!

94
00:31:14,890 --> 00:31:16,650
Don't be so cold!

95
00:31:16,650 --> 00:31:19,860
Let's be pals, Vega!

96
00:31:20,650 --> 00:31:22,940
Even my technology is still so far behind...

97
00:31:25,950 --> 00:31:27,620
This island is from the past.

98
00:31:28,620 --> 00:31:29,870
What?!

99
00:31:30,410 --> 00:31:32,250
What do you mean "from the past"?!

100
00:31:32,660 --> 00:31:35,460
What if I were to tell you...

101
00:31:36,080 --> 00:31:41,710
that 900 years ago, there was
an advanced kingdom like Egghead...?

102
00:31:41,710 --> 00:31:43,340
Would you believe me?

103
00:31:44,970 --> 00:31:46,880
Nine hundred years ago?!

104
00:31:46,880 --> 00:31:48,850
What are you talking about?!

105
00:31:54,180 --> 00:31:55,810
It's real!

106
00:31:55,810 --> 00:31:57,440
Look, Chopper!

107
00:31:57,440 --> 00:31:59,690
It's not a holo-holo!

108
00:32:00,020 --> 00:32:01,440
It's really there!

109
00:32:01,440 --> 00:32:02,690
It's made of iron!

110
00:32:05,700 --> 00:32:07,110
What is this?!

111
00:32:07,110 --> 00:32:08,660
It's pretty beat-up.

112
00:32:09,410 --> 00:32:11,370
Did it use to work?

113
00:32:11,870 --> 00:32:15,000
That would require futuristic technology.

114
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:16,830
Isn't it too old?

115
00:32:16,830 --> 00:32:18,580
I wanna ride it!

116
00:32:18,580 --> 00:32:20,590
Yeah, let's do it!

117
00:32:20,590 --> 00:32:22,340
Let's go, Chopper!

